## 5. Data Consistency & Validation

### 5.1 Firestore Rules Update

Add rules for goals and debts:

```
match /users/{uid}/goals/{goalId=**} {
  allow read: if request.auth.uid == uid;
  allow create: if request.auth.uid == uid && request.resource.data.uid == uid;
  allow update: if request.auth.uid == uid && resource.data.uid == uid;
  allow delete: if request.auth.uid == uid;
}

match /users/{uid}/debts/{debtId=**} {
  allow read: if request.auth.uid == uid;
  allow create: if request.auth.uid == uid && request.resource.data.uid == uid;
  allow update: if request.auth.uid == uid && resource.data.uid == uid;
  allow delete: if request.auth.uid == uid;
}
```

### 5.2 Frontend Validation

- Goal name and line items must have non-zero amounts.
- Debt must have a principal amount > 0.
- Debt type must be selected ("cash" or "existing").
- Repayment amount cannot exceed remaining balance (warning, but allow override).
- Recurring payment interval validation (next date must be in future).
- For cash debts, account selection on repayment is required.
- For existing debts, account selection on repayment is optional.

### 5.3 Computed Fields

Both `goals` and `debts` use denormalized fields (`totalAmount`, `currentBalance`, `totalRepaid`) for read performance. These are always recalculated during writes via `runTransaction()` to ensure consistency.

